Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:10.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}SOUND / A FIELD IN MOTION
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:10.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}An invisible journey
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.00,0:00:20.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Everything starts with vibration
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.00,0:00:20.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}A source disturbs its surroundings
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.00,0:00:30.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Follow one parcel of air
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.00,0:00:30.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}The marker shows its resting position
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.00,0:00:40.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Back and forth
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.00,0:00:40.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Displacement is exaggerated
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.00,0:00:50.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}The wave travels onward
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.00,0:00:50.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}The parcel stays near its equilibrium
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.00,0:01:00.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Local motion. Travelling energy.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.00,0:01:00.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}These are different movements
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.00,0:01:10.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Compression
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.00,0:01:10.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Parcels are closer together
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.00,0:01:20.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Rarefaction
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.00,0:01:20.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Parcels are farther apart
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.00,0:01:30.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}A longitudinal wave
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.00,0:01:30.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Motion is parallel to propagation
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.00,0:01:40.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Frequency sets the pace
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.00,0:01:40.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}More cycles per second: higher pitch
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.00,0:01:50.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Amplitude and intensity
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.00,0:01:50.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Greater pressure variation carries more intensity
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.00,0:02:00.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}One note. Different colours.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.00,0:02:00.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Harmonics shape timbre
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.00,0:02:10.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Sound needs a medium
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.00,0:02:10.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}No material medium: no ordinary sound
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.00,0:02:20.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Different media. Different speeds.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.00,0:02:20.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Elasticity and density both matter
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.00,0:02:30.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}At a stationary boundary
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.00,0:02:30.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Frequency stays. Wavelength can change.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.00,0:02:40.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}A surface splits the journey
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.00,0:02:40.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Reflection / transmission / absorption
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.00,0:02:50.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Reflection changes direction
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.00,0:02:50.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}A smooth surface redirects the wave
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.00,0:03:00.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Absorption is not soundproofing
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.00,0:03:00.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Reducing reflections does not guarantee isolation
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.00,0:03:10.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Sound spreads through openings
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.00,0:03:10.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Diffraction
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.00,0:03:20.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Compare opening and wavelength
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.00,0:03:20.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Width near one wavelength: strong spreading
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.00,0:03:30.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Geometry shapes the field
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.00,0:03:30.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}The parts of a wavefront interfere
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.00,0:03:40.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}When waves meet
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.00,0:03:40.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Pressure variations add
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.00,0:03:50.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}In phase
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.00,0:03:50.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Equal contributions reinforce
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.00,0:04:00.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Opposite phase
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.00,0:04:00.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Equal contributions can cancel locally
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.00,0:04:10.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}A small difference creates beats
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.00,0:04:10.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Nearby frequencies make the level pulse
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.00,0:04:20.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}A wave meets its reflection
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.00,0:04:20.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Standing patterns can form
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.00,0:04:30.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Nodes and antinodes
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.00,0:04:30.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Neighbouring nodes are half a wavelength apart
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.00,0:04:40.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Pressure is a different field
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.00,0:04:40.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Pressure and displacement nodes do not coincide
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.00,0:04:50.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Resonance selects frequencies
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.00,0:04:50.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Boundaries and damping matter
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.00,0:05:00.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}A room becomes part of the instrument
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.00,0:05:00.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Many reflections overlap
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.00,0:05:10.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Reverberation
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.00,0:05:10.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}A dense tail of decaying reflections
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.00,0:05:20.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Change the surfaces
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.00,0:05:20.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Absorption changes the decay
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.00,0:05:30.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Change the listening position
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.00,0:05:30.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Room modes can make bass uneven
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.00,0:05:40.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}A source in motion
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.00,0:05:40.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Each wavefront remembers its emission point
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.00,0:05:50.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Closer fronts ahead
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.00,0:05:50.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}An approaching source sounds higher
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.00,0:06:00.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Wider spacing behind
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.00,0:06:00.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}A receding source sounds lower
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.00,0:06:10.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}The medium still sets the wave speed
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.00,0:06:10.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Motion changes arrival timing
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.00,0:06:20.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}From air to hearing
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.00,0:06:20.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}The eardrum responds to pressure
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.00,0:06:30.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}The inner ear separates frequencies
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.00,0:06:30.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Different regions respond most strongly
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.00,0:06:40.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}The brain builds the experience
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.00,0:06:40.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Timing / spectrum / context
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.00,0:06:50.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}One connected story
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.00,0:06:50.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Vibration becomes a travelling disturbance
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.00,0:07:00.00,Title,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Sound transfers energy
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.00,0:07:00.00,Detail,,0,0,0,,{\fad(350,150)}Matter oscillates. The story travels.
